														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3827991">
									

<p>Well, see, the fact that they didn't shoot does make sense. What I can't parse is why they didn't do anything at all. Research and presumably security personnel were both there with her, but not a single person ran over to put hands on the SCP-3389-2 to punch it in what's left of its face? None of them tried to grab onto the doctor to pull her free? I mean, guns aren't their only option here, right?</p>
<p>If the -2 fended them off with unnatural strength or dragged her away too quickly for any of them to catch up, that would make sense. But from the looks of it, all these people just stood there with their fingers up their noses and watched it drag her off. I would readily upvote this if at least a single researcher had the presence of mind to run up to the monster, thwack it on the forehead with a ruler, and say &quot;NO! Bad dog!&quot;</p>

							</div>

								
					
